  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat Version: 2021.1.5p3\nDescription of the bug: Despite the belief with some of the audio having a memory leak, it seems as though, and apparently is a known about problem that Ram and Virtual Memory issues and likely some player crashes stem out of another source. Whenever an avatar loads in, it uses whatever memory available that it needs, yet when that avatar is unloaded, that data remains allocated and hardly if at all flushed out, and with that, builds up and up until one's system runs out of available memory, and not only crashes VRChat but can seize up the computer itself, as it did for me. In the testing we did, my memory usage ended up being 3 or 4GB higher than when we had started, despite it still only being us two with only two avatars loaded in at that point in time.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?): Go into a private instance, and have one person change to different avatars over and over again(perhaps an avatar world would be the best place to test). Your RAM/Virtual Memory usage will increase, and while it may slightly decrease, it will remain higher than it was before. If you went long enough, I would make the safe assumption it would give the same error that it had given me, which is attached below.\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots): An edited log file from the start of our testing with VRChat having been open in a public lobby prior to joining a private world, though I do not imagine that it would make a difference if you never went into a public world.\nhttps://pastebin.com/YGThJR15",
